WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 31 Leader Video
Unit 8, Lesson 3: Doubt

1
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.083
So years ago, when I was a high school student,

2
00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:12.370
I walked away from Christianity and went down

3
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.930
a whole other path for a good long time.

4
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:24.970
The primary reason that I walked away is because I had questions and I had doubts.

5
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:30.850
And you've gotten up to this point now where not only have you have all this content

6
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:34.250
and we've talked about love and we've talked about the power of questions and

7
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.050
the power of conversation.

8
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.877
But somewhere in there at some point, questions from others,

9
00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:44.290
information from other people,

10
00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:45.306
going to college,

11
00:00:45.306 --> 00:00:49.490
all kinds of different things are going to be coming at your students,

12
00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.430
causing doubt.

13
00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.570
What happens when they doubt?

14
00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.370
See I walked away because I thought well because I was doubting, I asked a question,

15
00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.170
I was told not to ask the questions.

16
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.170
I was told to just believe.

17
00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:09.709
I was told to just have faith and I didn't know what that even meant and I just

18
00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:10.270
couldn't

19
00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:17.270
figure it all out so I just said enough and I walked away.

20
00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:23.283
The statistics are still out there and they're still pretty prevalent that a large

21
00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:23.870
majority

22
00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:28.870
of students leave youth group after high school and there's a whole bunch of reasons

23
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.150
for that.

24
00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:36.750
One of them is because when they have doubts, they're not getting answered.

25
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.590
So this is an opportunity to open it up to your students and say listen, I get it.

26
00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:43.070
I know you have doubts.

27
00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:45.430
Maybe share some of your own and that's okay.

28
00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.430
Let's talk about it.

29
00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.830
Let's make sure this is an open forum.

30
00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:52.070
We talked weeks ago at the very beginning of this process.

31
00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:57.110
The idea of having an open communication and having a youth group that was very

32
00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:02.590
authentic and very open and invited the difficult questions.

33
00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.190
We talked about that those difficult questions were going to come.

34
00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:11.426
They're probably going to come even more now because sometimes the more information

35
00:02:11.426 --> 00:02:11.630
that

36
00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.590
you have, the more questions you have as a result.

37
00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:15.790
So invite those in.

38
00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:16.790
Invite those doubts.

39
00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:20.950
If students are not sure about Jesus, not sure about the existence of God, not sure

40
00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:25.910
about the biblical text, not sure about evil and pain and suffering, not sure about

41
00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.773
any of the things that we've talked about and maybe some things that we haven't

42
00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:28.990
talked

43
00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:33.380
about because there's a whole bunch of cultural issues that step into this that you

44
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:33.750
have to

45
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.030
help students navigate.

46
00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:42.317
And that's where helping students navigate doubt is an incredibly important thing,

47
00:02:42.317 --> 00:02:42.470
an

48
00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:46.950
important tool at actually furthering their faith because as they get those things

49
00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:55.790
answered, as they feel free to express those doubts, that tells them that as leaders

50
00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:00.110
we understand and that we've been there and that it's okay and we're going to walk

51
00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.790
with you through those.

52
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.616
So for the introduction activity this week,

53
00:03:04.616 --> 00:03:07.310
we asked students literally to write down

54
00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:09.870
one question that they've been wrestling with.

55
00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.694
Now you might as a large group activity, you know,

56
00:03:12.694 --> 00:03:14.670
you might actually take and compile

57
00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.150
some of those.

58
00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.870
You might do a Q&A session.

59
00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.630
I find Q&A sessions to be incredibly helpful.

60
00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:24.550
I open up the floor to students and just let them ask whatever they want.

61
00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.470
And yeah, you get some funny ones.

62
00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.670
I get a lot of like dinosaur questions and some interesting ones, you know,

63
00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:31.230
about Adam

64
00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.110
and Eve and some interesting, and those can be fun.

65
00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:38.190
You can play around with those a little bit and have some fun with it.

66
00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:42.230
But at the same time, some really good and profound questions will come up and the

67
00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:47.839
advantage to that is that if one student asks a question and another student's

68
00:03:47.839 --> 00:03:48.270
afraid

69
00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:53.710
to ask the same question, the student that was afraid gets their question answered.

70
00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.750
That can be an incredibly important and powerful tool.

71
00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:00.512
So I would encourage you to maybe do that this week or find a way to incorporate

72
00:04:00.512 --> 00:04:00.750
many

73
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.190
questions into your large group time.

74
00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:07.567
And then during small group time you can drill those questions down a little bit

75
00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:07.950
deeper.

76
00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:13.230
But make sure as you do that that your small group leaders are adequately prepared

77
00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.190
to handle some of the questions.

78
00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:19.550
Based on your situation and the leadership that you have in place and the volunteers

79
00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:24.870
that you have in place, just make sure that they are equipped to properly answer.

80
00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:28.270
And that remind them that it's okay, that they don't have an answer.

81
00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:34.990
To say I don't have an answer and to write those questions down and bring them back

82
00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:38.470
and find a way to get those questions answered specifically.

83
00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:44.590
Another important, powerful tool is your storyteller this week.

84
00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:49.864
To have somebody in front of your students that has actually expressed out and

85
00:04:49.864 --> 00:04:50.270
walked

86
00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:53.870
through it in some way, shape or form can be incredibly important.

87
00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.844
That story, whatever they've been through will resonate, I'm sure,

88
00:04:57.844 --> 00:04:59.470
with many of your students.

89
00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:03.630
So make sure that you don't need to find the best story or the biggest story

90
00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:07.270
or the most compelling story, but just so that students can see that, hey,

91
00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.190
I'm not the only one going through this.

92
00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:12.190
And I'm not the only one that has, I'm not the only student that's dealing with this

93
00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:16.359
and I'm not the only person that's ever dealt with this and people have got through

94
00:05:16.359 --> 00:05:16.510
it.

95
00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.470
Because some students might just have little questions here and there.

96
00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:23.750
Other students might be at a significant crisis of faith in their lives

97
00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.310
where they need serious direction.

98
00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.990
And after all that you've gone through in this study,

99
00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.981
some of those things may start to be, you know,

100
00:05:30.981 --> 00:05:32.590
coming up to the surface a little bit.

101
00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:39.070
So remind your students that no matter their questions, no matter the doubts,

102
00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:43.750
God can handle it and that He has given us everything we need

103
00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:49.870
to be entirely confident of who He is, who Jesus is, and what our salvation means.

